mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; 《基于口腔疾病的多学科教学I》是以小组讨论为主要教学形式的线上线下多学科整合式口腔医学本科专业必修课程，以交互、开放的形式实施学生的自主学习和合作学习。在给定教学案例的特定情境和问题下, 学生通过导师的引导,经过独立的学习、分析讨论,寻找解决问题的途径和答案。</p>
<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; 课程知识模块横向整合诊断学、内科学、外科学、口腔组织病理学、口腔材料学、口腔解剖生理学、头颈部局部解剖学、牙体牙髓病学、口腔修复学、口腔颌面外科学、牙周病学、口腔预防医学等基础与临床学科的知识关联，强调整体（口腔全科）医学、人文医学、健康管理与促进理念。以病种为基础设计4个教学案例 ,每个病案安排3次讨论课 (6学时)、一次案例总结课（1学时）。教学采用标准化的小组讨论模式，每个小组8-9名学生，共3个小组。通过案例分组讨论及资料收集，锻炼学生文献检索、归纳总结和综合理解能力，逻辑推理和口头表达能力，信息化手段运用的能力，自主学习、合作学习的能力等，为今后开展临床知识的学习打下良好基础。本课程学生学习效果考评由基于表现和能力的过程性评估（在线评估）、知识领会程度的结果性评估（书面考核）及出勤率三部分构成。</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:70.8500pt;">
                <td width=205 valign=center colspan=4 style="width:123.1000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">课程简介（英文）</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">Course </font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">Description</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span></span></b><b><span
                                    style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">(</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">in English</font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">)</span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><em>Multidisciplinary Teaching Based on Oral Diseases I</em>&nbsp;is an&nbsp;<strong>online-offline multidisciplinary integrated</strong>&nbsp;required course for undergraduate oral medicine majors,&nbsp;<strong>primarily conducted in a small-group discussion format</strong>. It facilitates student-directed and collaborative learning through an&nbsp;<strong>interactive and open format</strong>. Within the context of specific clinical scenarios and problems presented in teaching cases, students—guided by instructors—engage in&nbsp;<strong>independent study, analytical discussions</strong>, and the pursuit of solutions.</p>
<p>The course&nbsp;<strong>horizontally integrates knowledge</strong>&nbsp;across foundational and clinical disciplines including Diagnostics, Internal Medicine, Surgery, Oral Histopathology, Dental Materials Science, Oral Anatomy and Physiology, Regional Anatomy of Head and Neck, Cariology and Endodontics, Prosthodontics, Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery, Periodontology, and Preventive Dentistry. It emphasizes&nbsp;<strong>whole-person (comprehensive oral care) medicine, humanistic medicine, and concepts of health management and promotion</strong>.</p>
<p>Four disease-based teaching cases are designed, each comprising:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Three discussion sessions (6 credit hours)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>One case summary session (1 credit hour)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Instruction follows a&nbsp;<strong>standardized small-group discussion model</strong>, with&nbsp;<strong>three groups</strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>8–9 students each</strong>. Through case-based group discussions and research, the course cultivates students' abilities in:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Literature retrieval, summarization, and synthesis</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Logical reasoning and oral communication</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Application of information technology</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Self-directed and collaborative learning<br>This foundation prepares students for advanced clinical knowledge acquisition.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Assessment Structure:</strong><br>Student performance is evaluated through three components:</p>
<ol start="1">
<li>
<p><strong>Process-based assessment</strong>&nbsp;(performance and competency; online evaluation)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Outcome-based assessment</strong>&nbsp;(knowledge mastery; written examination)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Attendance rate</p>
</li>
</ol></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
